msgstr ""

msgid "Reload"
msgstr ""

msgid "Details"
msgstr ""

msgid "Compare"
msgstr ""

msgid "What changed between two conversations, by the questions you asked. Replies are not compared: the same question answered twice gives two different answers."
msgstr ""

msgid "Connections"
msgstr ""

msgid "Other apps and chat channels that can use Chronoa, and how to connect them. Read-only: nothing here starts anything."
msgstr ""

msgid "Conversations"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every saved conversation, newest first."
msgstr ""

msgid "Background mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Dashboards"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pages of charts Chronoa built. Ask it for a dashboard and it appears here; open one to see it in Chronoa's browser."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid "Is Chronoa actually hooked into this desktop right now? Every row is read from the thing that would make it true, and says which."
msgstr ""

msgid "Diagnostics"
msgstr ""

msgid "One question per row: is this part of Chronoa working right now, and if not, why not? Every answer is read from the module that would make the thing true. A row that could not be answered says so rather than showing a clean answer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Diff"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa changed on this machine, file by file, with line numbers. These writes already happened; to put one back, ask it to undo."
msgstr ""

msgid "Driving"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa can do with a mouse and a keyboard on this desktop, and where it has to say it cannot."
msgstr ""

msgid "Editor"
msgstr ""

msgid "Export"
msgstr ""

msgid "Chronoa keeps your conversation and your facts in your own data directory. These write them out as files you choose, and name what is in each one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Git"
msgstr ""

msgid "The repository Chronoa is working in, and the two git writes. Committing and pushing both ask in chat, behind their own switches."
msgstr ""

msgid "Goals"
msgstr ""

msgid "Plans Chronoa saved for later, one step at a time. Each step runs exactly as a chat request would, asking for the same things."
msgstr ""

msgid "Health"
msgstr ""

msgid "Whether Chronoa can see and drive this desktop, what the machine is reporting, and what it left running."
msgstr ""

msgid "The anatomy"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it has learned"
msgstr ""

msgid "Facts, which tools actually worked, and the two models fitted from them - with what each one can and cannot do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Transcribe"
msgstr ""

msgid "Machine"
msgstr ""

msgid "What this machine is doing, read once from its own machine-state senses. A sense that could not answer says so in its row; it is never shown as one that did."
msgstr ""

msgid "Meetings"
msgstr ""

msgid "Record a whole meeting, keep it, and read the transcript and notes back whenever you want them."
msgstr ""

msgid "What it remembers"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa has remembered: the facts you told it, and the readings its senses took. Nothing here reaches a model by being displayed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Answering now"
msgstr ""

msgid "Local state only. The cloud row is read from configuration and is never contacted; the two local probes ask a service running on this computer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Models"
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything Chronoa can run, what each one costs, and which are already here"
msgstr ""

msgid "What answers now and what is installed: the live answer first, the catalogue underneath."
msgstr ""

msgid "My files"
msgstr ""

msgid "Search your own documents and notes, by keyword and - where the embedding model is installed - by meaning."
msgstr ""

msgid "Notices"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa noticed on its own, newest first. Dismissing one keeps it from nagging again for the same thing."
msgstr ""

msgid "Privacy"
msgstr ""

msgid "What leaves this machine, and what Chronoa is allowed to read."
msgstr ""

msgid "Privacy & permissions"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa may read, do and send: the switches, the senses and the full consent table, in one place."
msgstr ""

msgid "What's running"
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything Chronoa started, and the button that stops each one. Nothing here runs unless you turned it on."
msgstr ""

msgid "Routines"
msgstr ""

msgid "One phrase that stands for a whole request. Say \"good morning\" and it asks for the weather, the day's calendar and the news - planned by the model like anything you typed, so every tool still meets its own gate."
msgstr ""

msgid "Sandbox"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where Chronoa runs commands, and a test of what they can reach."
msgstr ""

msgid "Senses"
msgstr ""

msgid "Every sense Chronoa has, and whether you have agreed to let it run. One switch per sense; a sense that is off is never invoked at all."
msgstr ""

msgid "What Chronoa can do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything Chronoa can be asked to do, read from the same live registry the model is handed. Each row says what it touches, a gate here writes the same key Settings does, and a row with a question offers it in the composer."
msgstr ""

msgid "Today"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reminders, alarms, timers, notes and to-dos on one page - what is due or waiting, read from the same stores the assistant uses. Only a timer can be changed here; the rest are started by asking."
msgstr ""

msgid "Triggers"
msgstr ""

msgid "The trigger rules this assistant could act on, read from the same two rule files the engines fire from. Arm or remove rules here; nothing on this page fires one."
msgstr ""

msgid "Speaking voice"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pick the voice Chronoa speaks with, hear it, and set its speed and pitch. Downloads open Setup on its Voice page."
msgstr ""

msgid "Workbench"
msgstr ""

msgid "Turn a command into a skill of your own, and see what that joined."
msgstr ""

msgid "Find something Chronoa can do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Jump to the newest message"
msgstr ""

msgid "What Shani Chronoa can do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Nothing matches. Try a shorter word."
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything Chronoa can do"
msgstr ""

msgid "What you can do"
msgstr ""

msgid "Get things done"
msgstr ""

msgid "Say what you want done, the way you would ask a person. Chronoa works out the steps, asks before anything that pays or deletes, and tells you what it did."
msgstr ""

msgid "Edit this and rerun from here"
msgstr ""

msgid "Everything after it is removed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ask something, or press the orb to speak."
msgstr ""

msgid "Ctrl+K for anything else  ·  Ctrl+F to find in this conversation  ·  ? for what Chronoa can do"
msgstr ""

